  overview: |
    Input contains 3-5 color "groups"; each group is either a SHAPE (vertices to be
    connected) or a DISTRACTOR (kept as-is). Some shapes carry a SHADOW in another
    color. Output connects vertices with straight H/V/diagonal(45°) rays and paints
    the shadow along a parallel copy of the shape.
  shape:
    vertices: 2-7 same-colored pixels in input; every consecutive pair along the
      polyline is strictly H, V, or 45° diagonal-aligned (equal abs dr/dc)
    topology: open polyline (2 endpoints) OR closed polygon (diamond/rect/pentagon)
      OR branching tree (one joint vertex with 3 incident edges) [observed]
    segments_per_shape: 1-7 straight segments, each length 2-13 cells
    output_fill: every cell on each segment painted with the shape color (vertices kept)
  shadow (optional, 0-2 per shape):
    trigger: one input pixel of a different color sits 8-adjacent to exactly one
      vertex v* of a shape; call that vertex the ANCHOR, and offset = shadow_pos - v*
      with offset in {-1,0,1}x{-1,0,1}\{(0,0)}
    output: for every cell (r,c) filled by the shape, also paint (r+dr, c+dc) with
      the shadow color, EXCEPT where the shape itself already occupies that cell
      (shape color wins on conflicts)
    nesting: a shadow color may itself have its own shadow (layered concentric copies) [observed]
  distractor (optional group, 0-1 groups, 1-3 pixels):
    a color whose input pixels are not H/V/diag alignable into a shape; kept unchanged
  counts_per_grid:
    shapes: 2-4 distinct color shape-groups
    shadows: 0-3 across all shapes
    distractor_groups: 0-1
  colors: drawn from {1,2,3,4,6,7,8}; each group uses a unique color
  spacing: shapes + shadows do not overlap each other's filled output cells except
    via the shadow priority rule; a >=1 cell background buffer between distinct groups [observed]
  diagram: |
    input:                   output:
    . 7 . . . 6 .            . 7 . . . 6 .     (6 apex + two endpoints drawn as V,
    . . . . . . .            . . 7 6 7 . .      7 traces parallel V offset (-1,-1))
    . . 6 . 6 . .            . 7 6 . 6 7 .
    . . . . . . .            7 6 . . . 6 7

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first — build the filled polyline shapes (with shadows) in the
    output canvas, then derive the input by keeping only vertex pixels (and the
    single shadow-anchor pixel) per group; distractors are identical in both.
  steps:
    - pick grid H,W in 15-22 and start with a blank canvas
    - decide shape_count in 2-4 and distinct shape colors from {1,2,3,4,6,7,8}
    - for each shape:
        pick vertex_count in 2-7 and topology (polyline | polygon | branching tree)
        place vertices so every connecting segment is strictly H/V/45°-diag aligned
          (construct by chaining random direction vectors with positive step length 2-13)
        paint every cell along each segment with the shape color
    - for 0-3 shapes (chosen randomly), attach a shadow:
        pick a vertex v* of the shape and an 8-neighbor offset (dr,dc) != (0,0)
        pick a new color (unused so far); for every cell (r,c) of the shape, paint
          (r+dr,c+dc) with shadow color if that cell is currently background (shape wins)
        optionally recurse: treat the shadow layer as a base and add a second shadow
    - with 50% chance add one distractor group: pick an unused color and 1-3 pixels
      placed so no two of them are H/V/diag aligned (or are too far to form a segment)
    - ensure pairwise >=1 cell buffer between filled regions of distinct groups; retry
      placement on conflict
    - derive input by copying output and erasing all non-vertex shape cells and all
      non-anchor shadow cells (keep vertices + one shadow-anchor pixel per shadow);
      distractor pixels are kept identically
    - sanity check: running a solver that connects same-color vertices via H/V/diag
      rays and shadows via (shadow_pos - nearest vertex) offset reproduces the output
